  "title": "Creation at an atom is decided by its cut",
  "subject": "What decides whether a removal creates at a line of a Fano atom",
  "conclusion": "For a Fano atom with its other elements present, whether a removal beyond one of its cuts creates at a line of it depends only on the patterns the removal's side allows on that cut's three ports: an emitter's lines receive iff the ports may be equal; a receiver's cut line iff the other two are not forced equal, its intact line iff the side tells the ports apart. Proved exhaustively over every port relation and deeper relation.",
